.Dd August 21, 2026
.Dt UMURMUR.CONF 5
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm umurmur.conf
.Nd uMurmur daemon configuration file
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file configures the
.Xr umurmurd 8
Mumble server.
.Pp
The following sections describe the available configuration parameters.
.Ss General Configuration
The following parameters may be specified at the top level of
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic max_bandwidth Ar bits/second
Maximum bandwidth available to a connected client.
The default is
.Qq 48000 .
.It Ic welcometext Ar text
Displayed to a client when it connects to the server.
The default is
.Qq Welcome to uMurmur!\&
.It Ic certificate Ar path
Certificate for TLS communication.
The default is
.Pa @CMAKE_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/umurmur/certificate.crt .
.It Ic private_key Ar path
Private key for TLS communication.
The default is
.Pa @CMAKE_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/umurmur/private_key.key .
.It Ic password Ar password
Server password required to connect.
An empty string disables the password.
The default is the empty string.
.It Ic max_users Ar number
Maximum number of simultaneous users.
The default is
.Qq 10 .
.It Ic bindaddr Ar address
IPv4 address on which the server listens.
The default is all available addresses.
.It Ic bindport Ar port
IPv4 listening port.
The default is
.Qq 64738 .
.It Ic bindaddr6 Ar address
IPv6 address on which the server listens.
The default is all available addresses.
.It Ic bindport6 Ar port
IPv6 listening port.
The default is
.Va bindport .
.It Ic admin_password Ar password
Password used for administrative functions.
If empty, administrative functions are disabled.
.It Ic ban_length Ar seconds
Length of time, in seconds, which a ban remains active.
A value of zero causes bans to remain indefinitely.
The default is zero.
.It Ic enable_ban Ar true/false
Enable client banning.
The default is
.Qq false .
.It Ic banfile Ar path
Path to the file used to store bans.
An empty string disables persistent ban storage.
The default is an empty string.
.It Ic sync_banfile Ar true/false
Synchronize the ban file when bans are modified.
If false, bans sync only when TERM is received.
The default is
.Qq false .
.It Ic allow_textmessage Ar true/false
Allow clients to send text messages.
The default is
.Qq true .
.It Ic show_addresses Ar true/false
Whether to show client's IP addresses under user information.
The default is
.Qq true .
.It Ic username Ar user
User to which the daemon drops privileges after reading the TLS
certificate and private key.
The account specified by
.Va username
must have permission to access
.Va logfile
and
.Va banfile .
.It Ic groupname Ar group
Group to which the daemon drops privileges.
If omitted, the primary group ID of
.Va username
is used.
.It Ic logfile Ar path
Path to a file to which log messages are written.
If omitted, log messages are sent to
.Xr syslog 3 .
.Pp
When
.Va logfile
is used, the file must be accessible by the user configured with
.Va username .
.It Ic ca_path Ar folder
CA location for CA-signed certificates.
The default is unset.
.It Ic default_channel Ar channel
Name of the channel in which newly connected users are placed.
The default is the root channel.
.El
.Ss Channel Configuration
Channels are declared in the
.Va channels
configuration list.
Each channel requires
.Va name
and
.Va parent
parameters.
.Pp
The following parameters are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic name Ar text
Name displayed to clients.
.It Ic parent Ar channel
Name of the parent channel.
.It Ic noenter Ar true/false
Prevent clients from entering the channel.
The default is
.Qq false .
This can be used to create a folder channel containing other channels.
.It Ic password Ar password
Password required to enter the channel.
The default is an empty string.
.It Ic description Ar text
Description displayed for the channel.
The default is an empty string.
.It Ic silent Ar true/false
Prevent speech from being transmitted in the channel.
The default is
.Qq false .
.It Ic position Ar index
Integer controlling the channel's position in the client's channel tree.
The default is zero.
When channels have the same position, they are sorted alphabetically.
.It Ic allow_temp Ar true/false
Allow temporary subchannels to be created below this channel.
The default is
.Qq false .
.El
.Ss Channel Links
Channel links are declared in the
.Va channel_links
configuration list.
A channel link performs one-way duplication of speech
from one channel to another.
.Pp
Both of the following parameters are required:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic source Ar channel
Name of the source channel.
.It Ic destination Ar channel
Name of the destination channel.
.El
.Pp
Speech transmitted in the source channel is also transmitted in the
destination channel.
The link is one-way; speech originating in the destination channel
is not sent back to the source channel.
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A configuration might look like:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
username = "umurmur";
groupname = "umurmur";

certificate = "@CMAKE_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/umurmur/certificate.crt";
private_key = "@CMAKE_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/umurmur/private_key.key";

default_channel = "Lobby";
channels = (
	{
		name = "Root";
		parent = "";
		description = "Root channel. No entry.";
		noenter = true;
	},
	{
		name = "Lobby";
		parent = "Root";
		description = "Lobby channel";
	},
	{
		name = "Silent";
		parent = "Root";
		description = "Silent channel";
		silent = true;
	},
	{
		name = "Red team";
		parent = "Lobby";
		description = "The Red team channel";
		position = 0;
		password = "redpw";
		allow_temp = true;
	},
	{
		name = "Blue team";
		parent = "Lobby";
		description = "The Blue team channel";
		position = 1;
		password = "bluepw";
	}
);

channel_links = (
	{
		source = "Lobby";
		destination = "Red team";
	},
	{
		source = "Lobby";
		destination = "Blue team";
	}
);
.Ed
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr umurmurd 8
.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
.An Martin Johansson Aq Mt martin@fatbob.nu
and
.An Thorvald Natvig Aq Mt thorvald@natvig.com .
